Date:   Thu Oct 29 23:15:53 2026 -0600

    gateway: a refusal asked earlier is told over the last member's allowance error
    
    When every member of a group failed, the earlier members refusing the
    request and the last one out of its allowance or credit, the agent was
    handed the last member's 429/403 (on Kiro: "usage limit reached ...
    (MONTHLY_REQUEST_COUNT)"), which agents read as the provider being out
    of quota or the sign-in being bad. The refusal branch never set
    `other`, so the end-of-request branch that prefers an earlier
    non-allowance failure didn't fire (#4031, SunflowersLwtech; seen
    again on a Kiro group where six accounts refused and the seventh was
    used up).
    
    The first refusal is now kept in a variable of its own and told, as
    `refusedStatus` (400) with its words, in that same branch when nothing
    of the last reply went out (`!hw.passing`). It isn't put in `other`:
    that would make `newHoldWriter` hold the last member's streamed reply
    on every request where someone refused, and most of those end 200.
    
    Verified: TestRefusalEarlierWinsOverTheLastAllowance (quota 429 and
    credit 403 as the last member) fails without the change:
      refusal_earlier_test.go:35: 429 {"error":{..."message":"B: usage limit
      reached: You have reached the limit. (MONTHLY_REQUEST_COUNT)",...}}
      refusal_earlier_test.go:35: 403 {"error":{..."message":"B: Student plan
      credits consumed.",...}}
    go test ./internal/gateway/ -run 'Refus|Probe|Rest|Earlier', go vet
    ./internal/gateway/ and gofmt pass.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

