tes a refusal before any of the reply is asked of is Settings' `RefusalRetries` (`refusalAsksAgain`, counted per request in the candidate loop; a group's other members count too): unset, every one left (#248); 0, none (#1925, DD on Discord). When nobody is left, an agent on Anthropic's Messages API gets the held refusal itself, the vendor's 200 with `stop_reason` `refusal` and its `stop_details`, streamed or whole (`holdWriter.handBack`), since that is what Claude Code switches to its fallback model on; a 400 is only an API error to it. Codex and Chat clients still get `failTo`'s 400 (`refusedStatus`), which they don't ask again for. `TestRefusalRetries*` in [`refusal_retries_test.go`](../../internal/gateway/refusal_retries_test.go) cover keys, a group and the Claude subscription. The ChatGPT backend's 502 "response protection is unavailable" is about the request's content, not the account: the same history fails the same on each of its accounts and models. It rests nobody, isn't tried again after a moment, and isn't asked of the provider's other accounts or models; another provider left in a group is asked once (`protectionRefused`, `elsewhere`). One cause is known (#1270): a history that replays the backend's own `web_search_call` in a request that doesn't declare the `web_search` tool is refused so, whatever the account, model or turn (a plain turn, a thread's description, a compaction, Codex's own text compaction for a custom provider with `tools: []`). Every request to the ChatGPT backend with such a history therefore declares cached-only search (`{"type":"web_search","external_web_access":false}`, `provider.DeclareSearch`): an account's in `codexBody`, Codex's own sign-in relayed in `codexUpstreamOn`. It goes in the tools, or for Responses Lite (its header, `reasoning.context` `all_turns`, or an `additional_tools` item already there), which refuses a top-level `web_search`, in the `additional_tools` item. A request that offered no tools gets `tool_choice` `non